1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,912
Aziz still has a phone number that he has not used since university.

2
00:00:03,962 --> 00:00:08,088
He gave it to the state services portal years ago, and then he forgot it.

3
00:00:08,138 --> 00:00:09,960
MyID did not forget.

4
00:00:10,010 --> 00:00:15,752
His face passed MyID in the lift, so whose phone number is on his record?

5
00:00:15,802 --> 00:00:22,328
That old number now sits inside his verified identity, behind the one closed door of Lesson 14.

6
00:00:22,378 --> 00:00:28,856
The money for his mother still waits, and one step stands between Aziz and level two: the phone check.

7
00:00:28,906 --> 00:00:31,376
Level two means two things at once.

8
00:00:31,426 --> 00:00:35,816
MyID proved the person, and the phone number of the account belongs to that person.

9
00:00:35,866 --> 00:00:37,880
A face proves who holds the phone.

10
00:00:37,930 --> 00:00:40,352
It does not prove that the number is his.

11
00:00:40,402 --> 00:00:46,232
Picture a man who gets a SIM card with a stranger's number, and passes MyID with his own face.

12
00:00:46,282 --> 00:00:50,720
Without a phone check, he would get level two on a number that belongs to somebody else.

13
00:00:50,770 --> 00:00:54,944
So, after Aziz confirms his data, the phone check starts.

14
00:00:54,994 --> 00:01:02,864
Step one: the platform sends TAF a face confirmation, with his personal identification number and his phone number.

15
00:01:02,914 --> 00:01:07,568
The platform sends it, so the app never sees the personal identification number.

16
00:01:07,618 --> 00:01:13,856
Step two: the platform compares his phone number with the number from MyID, as full international numbers.

17
00:01:13,906 --> 00:01:19,664
When they are the same, the status is Confirmed, and the platform asks TAF nothing more.

18
00:01:19,714 --> 00:01:24,584
But Aziz's numbers differ: the MyID one is his old university number.

19
00:01:24,634 --> 00:01:28,064
The next step also runs when MyID gives no number at all.

20
00:01:28,114 --> 00:01:36,176
Step three: the platform asks TAF one question: does this phone number belong to this personal identification number?

21
00:01:36,226 --> 00:01:40,784
TAF compares the number with the personal identification number from step one.

22
00:01:40,834 --> 00:01:42,656
Owner gives Confirmed.

23
00:01:42,706 --> 00:01:45,608
Not owner closes the record at level one.

24
00:01:45,658 --> 00:01:50,096
Account not found, or no answer from TAF, gives Processing.

25
00:01:50,146 --> 00:01:52,952
Today, TAF says owner.

26
00:01:53,002 --> 00:01:56,792
His status is Confirmed, and Aziz is at level two.

27
00:01:56,842 --> 00:02:01,880
The bank gets an event that his identity is verified, with no personal data in it.

28
00:02:01,930 --> 00:02:05,312
Now suppose that TAF had said: not owner.

29
00:02:05,362 --> 00:02:10,568
Then the number belongs to somebody else, and the platform closes his record at level one.

30
00:02:10,618 --> 00:02:17,696
It sends an SMS to the number that says the number is not his, and it counts a failed attempt for the number and the phone.

31
00:02:17,746 --> 00:02:20,912
Now suppose that TAF had given no answer.

32
00:02:20,962 --> 00:02:24,488
His status would be Processing, and he would stay at level one.

33
00:02:24,538 --> 00:02:26,600
The app shows him the word Processing.

34
00:02:26,650 --> 00:02:31,688
The platform opens a phone review, and sends an event to the bank's antifraud system.

35
00:02:31,738 --> 00:02:41,816
The review shows an operator his phone number, his personal identification number masked, the MyID number masked except the last four digits, the time, the device and the app.

36
00:02:41,866 --> 00:02:46,280
There is no timer: Aziz stays at level one until a person decides.

37
00:02:46,330 --> 00:02:53,216
Processing is an honest state: the platform admits that it does not know, and waits for a person instead of a guess.

38
00:02:53,266 --> 00:02:58,472
Operators get no message for each review; they watch the review list in the admin panel.

39
00:02:58,522 --> 00:03:04,568
When a review stays open longer than the configured age, the platform sends an alert to operations.

40
00:03:04,618 --> 00:03:08,480
The operator approves or rejects, and must write a reason.

41
00:03:08,530 --> 00:03:12,152
An approval starts only after a second operator agrees.

42
00:03:12,202 --> 00:03:15,344
Then Aziz gets level two, as with Confirmed.

43
00:03:15,394 --> 00:03:22,808
A rejection starts at once: it closes his record at level one, and he gets the SMS that the number is not his.

44
00:03:22,858 --> 00:03:25,064
Both decisions go to the audit trail.

45
00:03:25,114 --> 00:03:27,800
Back to the real Aziz, who is confirmed.

46
00:03:27,850 --> 00:03:32,456
His record keeps each check of his number, with the provider, the app and the time.

47
00:03:32,506 --> 00:03:39,008
A code through TAF, in the mobile bank, at his registration on Sunday of the first week.

48
00:03:39,058 --> 00:03:41,840
A MyID check today, which gave a different number.

49
00:03:41,890 --> 00:03:45,152
And the owner answer from TAF, a moment later.

50
00:03:45,202 --> 00:03:48,416
So the bank can always show how it knows that this number is his.

51
00:03:48,466 --> 00:03:50,288
Now a check for you.

52
00:03:50,338 --> 00:03:59,224
Suppose MyID had given the same number that Aziz has on his phone: does the platform still ask TAF who owns it?

53
00:03:59,274 --> 00:04:07,984
No: the same number gives Confirmed at once, and the platform asks TAF only when the numbers differ or MyID has no number.

54
00:04:08,034 --> 00:04:10,936
The phone check proves that the number belongs to the person.

55
00:04:10,986 --> 00:04:17,536
It compares the number from MyID first, and asks TAF only when that number is different or missing.

56
00:04:17,586 --> 00:04:24,808
Owner gives level two, not owner closes the record at level one, and no answer opens a phone review.

57
00:04:24,858 --> 00:04:28,792
An approval needs two operators, and a rejection needs one.

58
00:04:28,842 --> 00:04:33,928
Aziz is at level two, and the money for his mother is one step closer.

59
00:04:33,978 --> 00:04:38,608
Lesson 16 shows how his phone becomes the one phone that can move money.
